==Season Summary==
Once more, the eighteen new contestants were divided into three new tribes of six: [[Hina]], [[Kele]], and [[Uli]]. Kele struggled almost immediately, losing the first three [[Immunity Challenge]]s and their physically strongest member, [[Jake Latimer|Jake]], to a non-lethal snakebite. In contrast, Hina and Uli worked more smoothly, though the latter tribe suffered from personality clashes, most notably between [[Jawan Pitts|Jawan]] and [[Savannah Louie|Savannah]], and eventually [[Sage Ahrens-Nichols|Sage]] and [[Shannon Fairweather|Shannon]].

One week into the game, the castaways were surprised by a [[Tribe Switch|tribe switch]] that split them between Kele and Hina. Old tribal lines largely held, and the original Uli members on the new Hina used their numbers advantage to vote out the original Hina players. While these divisions seemed firm heading into a second tribe switch on Day 11, Jawan and Sage aligned with original Hina member [[Steven Ramm|Steven]] to blindside Sage's rival, Shannon, just shy of the [[merge]].

On Day 13, the tribes merged into the [[Lewatu]] tribe. The original Hina, now joined by Jawan and Sage, gained early control by blindsiding [[Nate Moore|Nate]] at the first merged [[Tribal Council]], leaving the remainder of his [[Uli Alliance|alliance]] ([[Rizo Velovic|Rizo]], Savannah, and [[Sophi Balerdi|Sophi]]) on the bottom. However, a mix of Rizo's defensive use of his [[Hidden Immunity Idol]], Savannah's strong performances in Immunity Challenges, and the opposing group's poor coordination allowed the trio to slowly chip away at their rivals, reducing them to only [[Kristina Mills|Kristina]], Sage, and Steven by the final six.

With the game at an apparent 3â€“3 stalemate on Day 22, Steven found a [[Vote Blocker]] advantage and hoped to use it to swing the upcoming vote in his side's favor. After learning this, Sophi planned to steal the advantage at Tribal Council using her [[Knowledge is Power Advantage]], which she had found on Hina. However, Steven blocked Savannah's vote before Tribal Council, making Sophi's advantage useless and seemingly ensuring her elimination. Instead, Kristina and Sage unexpectedly turned on Steven, and he was voted out unanimously. 

Betraying Steven proved to be a fatal error for Kristina, who was unanimously voted out at the final five for being the tribe's best fire-maker. Sophi then won the [[Final Immunity Challenge]] and, despite her close ties with Savannah and Rizo, chose to take Sage to the [[Final Three]], forcing her allies to compete in the fire-making challenge. Savannah won and joined the other two women in the end.

At the [[Final Tribal Council]], Sophi emphasized her survival skills and reaching the end without idols or immunity wins. Savannah highlighted her adaptability and challenge wins, though she faced criticism for struggling to connect with some jurors. Sage spoke about playing an emotional and authentic game, but was criticized for her betrayals. In the end, the [[jury]] most respected Savannah's overall game, awarding her the title of [[Sole Survivor]] in a 5-2-1 vote.

