==Trivia==
* ''Survivor 49'' is one of four seasons, alongside {{S2|19}}, {{S2|25}}, and {{S2|33}}, to have contestants return for another season before their original season aired.
* ''Survivor 49'' is the fourth season, following {{S2|29}}, {{S2|31}}, and {{S2|34}} to have castaways with homophonic first names (names that are pronounced the same, but spelled differently), namely [[Sophi Balerdi]] and [[Sophie Segreti]].
* ''Survivor 49'' contains the most known alternates of any cast, whether they were for previous seasons or this season, with 4: Jason, MC, Sage, and Sophie.
* ''Survivor 49'' is the first season where every castaway who reached the [[merge]] was part of at least two different pre-merge [[tribe]]s.
* ''Survivor 49'' is the first season to not have any players use their [[Shot in the Dark]] since it was introduced in {{S2|41}}.
* ''Survivor 49'' is the first season since {{S2|40}} to have only two active tribes at once.
* ''Survivor 49'' is the first season since ''Winners at War'' to not feature the [[Earn the Merge]] twist.
* ''Survivor 49'' is the first season since ''San Juan del Sur'' to feature an all-female [[Final Tribal Council]], and the third time it has happened with a Final Three.
* ''Survivor 49'' is the first season since {{S2|39}} where the 1st runner up and the Sole Survivor are same gender.
* Every person that won individual immunity had their name start with the letter 'S'.
* The castaways who made Final Tribal Council all had names starting with the letter 'S'.

